{
  "name": "Google Cloud (legacy)",
  "description": "Google's pre-2026 Cloud Platform icon set. 216 product marks in flat two-tone vector, still the ones most architecture diagrams use.",
  "source": "Google Cloud",
  "sourceUrl": "https://cloud.google.com/icons",
  "license": "Google Cloud Platform icons, redistributed under Google's terms of use",
  "accent": "#4285F4",
  "order": 10,
  "tags": [
    "gcp",
    "google cloud"
  ],
  "_styling_note": "How this set opens, and the preset buttons in the styling sidebar. Both are patches over the app-wide defaults, so only the fields that differ need stating. Flat two-tone product marks read best with the hand-drawn label font they will sit next to on a canvas, in the blue that dominates the artwork.",
  "defaults": {
    "showLabel": false,
    "labelFontFamily": 5,
    "labelFontSize": 18,
    "labelColor": "#4285f4",
    "iconScale": 1
  },
  "presets": [
    {
      "id": "default",
      "label": "Default",
      "hint": "Just the marks - no label, no frame"
    },
    {
      "id": "labelled",
      "label": "Labelled",
      "hint": "Each mark with its product name underneath",
      "options": {
        "showLabel": true,
        "showCard": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sketch",
      "label": "Sketch",
      "hint": "Hand-drawn hatched frame, matches a sketched diagram",
      "_note": "cardBgColor is a tint rather than transparent: hachure is stroked in the background colour, so this preset drew no hatch at all while it was transparent - and drew an unreadable slab when it was the full accent. Excalidraw's own palette pairs a saturated stroke with a pale fill for exactly this reason. iconRoughness is deliberately lower than cardRoughness: a frame can be scribbled without the artwork inside it losing its shape.",
      "options": {
        "showCard": true,
        "showLabel": true,
        "cardCorners": "square",
        "cardStrokeWidth": 1,
        "cardFillStyle": "hachure",
        "cardBgColor": "#e8f0fe",
        "cardStrokeColor": "#4285f4",
        "cardRoughness": 2,
        "iconRoughness": 1,
        "padding": 12
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dark-card",
      "label": "Dark card",
      "hint": "Soft dark panel for dark canvases",
      "options": {
        "showCard": true,
        "showLabel": true,
        "cardCorners": "rounded",
        "cardStrokeWidth": 1,
        "cardFillStyle": "solid",
        "cardBgColor": "rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.8)",
        "cardStrokeColor": "#4285f4",
        "cardRoughness": 0,
        "labelColor": "#f8fafc",
        "padding": 12
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "light-card",
      "label": "Light card",
      "hint": "Clean white panel for printed diagrams",
      "options": {
        "showCard": true,
        "showLabel": true,
        "cardCorners": "rounded",
        "cardStrokeWidth": 1,
        "cardFillStyle": "solid",
        "cardBgColor": "#ffffff",
        "cardStrokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
        "cardRoughness": 0,
        "labelColor": "#1e293b",
        "padding": 12
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "outline",
      "label": "Outline",
      "hint": "Unfilled frame, keeps the canvas showing through",
      "options": {
        "showCard": true,
        "showLabel": true,
        "cardCorners": "square",
        "cardStrokeWidth": 2,
        "cardFillStyle": "solid",
        "cardBgColor": "transparent",
        "cardStrokeColor": "#4285f4",
        "cardRoughness": 0,
        "padding": 12
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tight",
      "label": "Tight",
      "hint": "Frame fitted to the artwork rather than its viewBox",
      "options": {
        "showCard": true,
        "showLabel": true,
        "cardCorners": "rounded",
        "cardStrokeWidth": 1,
        "cardFillStyle": "solid",
        "cardBgColor": "transparent",
        "cardStrokeColor": "#4285f4",
        "cardRoughness": 0,
        "fitFrame": true,
        "padding": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "large",
      "label": "Large",
      "hint": "Double size for a title or a legend",
      "options": {
        "iconScale": 2,
        "showLabel": true,
        "labelFontSize": 24
      }
    }
  ],
  "_categories_note": "Six display buckets. Ten was too many to scan: the chip bar overflowed at every viewport width and four buckets held under twenty icons each, so the filter mostly told you which of ten near-synonymous labels Google had picked. The ten fine-grained matchers still exist below in `rules` - merging their keyword lists would change first-wins precedence and silently reclassify icons that are currently correct.",
  "categories": [
    {
      "id": "ai-ml",
      "name": "AI & ML",
      "description": "Vertex AI, AutoML, Dialogflow, Speech & Vision APIs",
      "color": "#8AB4F8"
    },
    {
      "id": "compute",
      "name": "Compute",
      "description": "GKE, Compute Engine, Cloud Run, Functions, Apigee, Workflows",
      "color": "#81C995"
    },
    {
      "id": "data",
      "name": "Data & Storage",
      "description": "BigQuery, Dataflow, Cloud Storage, Spanner, Firestore",
      "color": "#FDE293"
    },
    {
      "id": "network-security",
      "name": "Network & Security",
      "description": "VPC, Load Balancing, DNS, IAM, KMS, BeyondCorp",
      "color": "#C58AF9"
    },
    {
      "id": "operations",
      "name": "Operations",
      "description": "Logging, Monitoring, Billing, Cloud Build, Artifact Registry",
      "color": "#9BBBD4"
    },
    {
      "id": "general",
      "name": "General",
      "description": "Marketplace, Healthcare, Maps, Gaming, IoT",
      "color": "#BDC1C6"
    }
  ],
  "_rules_note": "Ordered, first-wins, tested as substrings against the lowercased filename. Order is load-bearing: 'access' would swallow half the networking bucket if it ran earlier, and 'api' must run after the AI and compute buckets. Anything unmatched falls through to the category with no rules, i.e. 'general'.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "category": "ai-ml",
      "match": [
        "ai",
        "automl",
        "dialogflow",
        "speech",
        "translation",
        "vision",
        "natural-language",
        "agent",
        "nlp",
        "tensorflow",
        "datalab",
        "inference",
        "recommendations",
        "retail-api"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "compute",
      "match": [
        "compute",
        "kubernetes",
        "gke",
        "anthos",
        "app-engine",
        "cloud-run",
        "bare-metal",
        "vmware",
        "container",
        "gpu",
        "tpu",
        "kuberun",
        "batch",
        "quantum"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "data",
      "match": [
        "storage",
        "sql",
        "spanner",
        "bigtable",
        "datastore",
        "firestore",
        "memorystore",
        "filestore",
        "disk",
        "database",
        "ssd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "data",
      "match": [
        "bigquery",
        "dataflow",
        "dataproc",
        "dataprep",
        "dataplex",
        "datapol",
        "looker",
        "pubsub",
        "data-studio",
        "analytics",
        "data-catalog",
        "data-loss",
        "datashare",
        "data-transfer",
        "data-qna",
        "insights"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "network-security",
      "match": [
        "dns",
        "cdn",
        "load-balancing",
        "nat",
        "vpn",
        "vpc",
        "virtual-private",
        "interconnect",
        "router",
        "routes",
        "network",
        "connectivity",
        "traffic",
        "firewall",
        "ip-addresses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "network-security",
      "match": [
        "identity",
        "iam",
        "security",
        "secret",
        "armor",
        "key",
        "kms",
        "beyondcorp",
        "binary-authorization",
        "certificate",
        "ekm",
        "hsm",
        "ids",
        "phishing",
        "risk",
        "assured",
        "access",
        "permissions",
        "iap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "compute",
      "match": [
        "apigee",
        "api",
        "gateway",
        "connector",
        "eventarc",
        "workflow",
        "tasks",
        "scheduler",
        "composer",
        "functions",
        "endpoints"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "operations",
      "match": [
        "logging",
        "monitoring",
        "ops",
        "stackdriver",
        "trace",
        "debugger",
        "profiler",
        "error-reporting",
        "os-",
        "billing",
        "asset",
        "audit",
        "quotas",
        "policy",
        "dashboard",
        "gce-systems"
      ]
    },
    {
      "category": "operations",
      "match": [
        "build",
        "code",
        "deploy",
        "registry",
        "shell",
        "powershell",
        "release-notes"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "_synonyms_note": "Bidirectional search aliases: any term in a group finds any other, so the Virtual Private Cloud icon answers to 'vpc' and 'vpc' answers to the full name. Matched whole-word against the normalised filename and title, which is why 'ids' does not fire on 'identity'.",
